# CyberGuard — Custom Suricata detection rules (local lab)
#
# NOTE: As of Phase 2 the active source-of-truth rules file is
# `cyberguard.rules` (loaded by Suricata on the Kali VM). This file is kept as a
# placeholder/scratch space and is not referenced by the VM configuration.
#
# These rules run inside Suricata, the ONLY detection engine in this project.
# They are authored and tested against authorized, controlled lab traffic using
# harmless HTTP markers. No live rules are defined yet — rule authoring is a
# later phase.
#
# Conventions:
#   - Use the local signature ID (sid) range: >= 1000000 to avoid clashing with
#     rules shipped by Suricata / rule providers.
#   - Keep each rule commented with its purpose and the lab traffic that
#     triggers it.
#
# Example (DISABLED — for reference only, enabled in a later phase):
# alert http any any -> any any (msg:"CYBERGUARD Lab HTTP marker"; \
#     content:"CYBERGUARD-LAB-TEST"; http.uri; sid:1000001; rev:1;)
